*.iml
.gradle/
/gradle/
/local.properties
/.idea/
.DS_Store
/build/
/captures
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
*.ap_
*.dex
*.class
*.jar
# ...except the Gradle wrapper jar, which MUST be committed: without it
# `./gradlew` dies with "Unable to access jarfile" on a fresh clone. Gradle's
# own docs: "To make the Wrapper files available to other developers and
# execution environments, you need to check them into version control …
# Adding the JAR file to version control is expected."
# `**/` so it covers examples/ too. Regenerate only via
# `gradle wrapper --gradle-version X`; never merge an external wrapper diff.
!**/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar
*.log
/sdk/build/
/sdk/.cxx/

# Native shared libraries are build artifacts — only .gitkeep is tracked
*.so

# Origon workspace agent files — internal team/agent memory, kept LOCAL ONLY.
# This is a PUBLIC repo: these must never be published. (See ws/CLAUDE.md.)
/CLAUDE.md
/CONTRACT.md
/RULES.md
/TODO.md
/LOG.md
